16z7|n|That which lubricates; specifically, a substance, as oil, grease, plumbago, etc., used for reducing the friction of the working parts of machinery.	a:mfu,84,3;vdr,45,4~vdr,45,4;mfu,84,3
1703|n|That which happens to a person; an event, good or ill, affecting one's interests or happiness, and which is deemed casual; a course or series of such events regarded as occurring by chance; chance; hap; fate; fortune; often, one's habitual or characteristic fortune; as, good, bad, ill, or hard luck. Luck is often used for good luck; as, luck is better than skill.	a:60f,42,5;7ey,28,5;vdr,24,6;1b5y,18,4;1awf,13,7~1awf,13,7;vdr,24,6;60f,42,5;7ey,28,5;1b5y,18,4	V:up1,37,4;26ev,25,7;1lmu,6,4~26ev,25,7;up1,37,4;1lmu,6,4
